// Title: Winlogon Notify Key Logon Persistence
// Sigma ID: bbf59793-6efb-4fa1-95ca-a7d288e52c88
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-12-30 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1547.004
// Description: Adversaries may abuse features of Winlogon to execute DLLs and/or executables when a user logs
//   in. Winlogon.exe is a Windows component responsible for actions at logon/logoff as well as the
//   secure attention sequence (SAS) triggered by Ctrl-Alt-Delete.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1547.004/T1547.004.md#atomic-test-3---winlogon-notify-key-logon-persistence---powershell
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_winlogon_notify_key.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\Notify\\logon" and RegistryValueData endswith ".dll"
